\section{Introduction}

Many students email me about why they haven't received the grades for the 
course prgi, for example prgi25.
The cause is always the same: they have not submitted or presented or passed 
all the assignments.

For this reason, I wrote the [[canvaslms results --missing]] functionality.
On this course we have four modules:
\begin{itemize}
\item KAL1 covering Excel,
\item LAB1 covering the labs,
\item LAB2 covering the exam Datorprovet,
\item LAB3 covering the project and a final diagnostic test.
\end{itemize}
Each module exists under that name in Ladok and has a corresponding assignment 
group in Canvas.
A missing grade for LAB3 in Ladok means that one of the assignments in the 
assignment group LAB3 in Canvas lacks a passing grade.

Most students who email me have missed the final diagnostic test, which is the 
last assignment in the course that must be done earliest the last week of the 
course.
That is part of LAB3.

We can run
\begin{minted}{bash}
canvaslms results --missing -c prgi25 -A LAB3 \
  -S canvaslms.grades.conjunctavgsurvey
\end{minted}
to get a list of all students and what they are missing, one assignment and a 
motivation per row.
We need the [[-S]] option to specify a summary module that can handle the 
survey included in LAB3.
For example, if we pipe the output of the command to [[cut -f 1,2,4-]], to 
remove student identifiers, the output looks like this:
